        "label": "Upload a file to a signed storage slot",
        "job": "Upload one file from a folder the person granted to a signed storage slot a page hands over, only to a destination the tool's own list allows, so the page never sees the file",
        "description": "Give file (its name inside the folder the person granted this tool, such as reports/diag.zip), content_type (the file's media type) and slot ({ url, fields }: the https address and the text form fields the storage service signed). The slot is checked as a whole before a byte leaves: https, a host equal to a destination row's, a path inside that row's folder, no query, fragment, credentials or port, text-only fields within the row's field cap, and a content type the row lists. The file is read from the granted folder only (a name that leaves it, or a link out of it, names nothing), held once, and posted as the form's last field. Storage redirects are refused, so the file is not forwarded to another address. Returns sent, size and said; the signed fields are never in an answer or an error. The shipped destination list is empty, so it uploads nowhere until a destination row is added to read-data/guarded-upload.json.",
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "file",
            "content_type",
            "slot"
          ],
